# Nirva AI Brain Operating System

## Vision

Nirva AI Workspace = **AI Brain Marketplace** + **Agent Workforce** + **Executive Dashboard** + **Coding Workspace**

Not a chatbot. An operating system for AI-era work.

## Core concepts

| Concept | File | Description |
|---------|------|-------------|
| Brain Category | `shared/brains.ts` | CEO, CTO, Developer, Marketing, Data, Voice, Vision |
| AI Brain | `AI_BRAINS[]` | Marketplace item — category + agents + models + plan |
| Global Provider | `GLOBAL_PROVIDERS[]` | OpenAI, DeepSeek, Mistral, Qwen, etc. by region |
| Brain Router | `planBrainTeam(message)` | Intent → brain categories → agent team |
| Model ROUTER | `shared/model-orchestration.ts` | Existing — picks model tier within brain |
| Pricing | `PRICING_PLANS` | free (OSS) / pro (per-brain) / enterprise |

## Pipeline

```
User → DESK (intent) → Brain Router (planBrainTeam) → Model ROUTER → Agent Team → Report
```

## API

- `GET /api/brains?plan=free|pro|enterprise`
- `GET /api/brains/categories`
- `GET /api/brains/providers?region=usa`
- `GET /api/brains/pricing`
- `POST /api/brains/plan` `{ message }` → BrainTeamPlan

## UI

- `/brains` — Brain Marketplace + router demo
- Future: Morning Briefing on Home, `/workspace` coding pipeline

## When adding a brain

1. Add to `BRAIN_CATEGORIES` if new category
2. Add `AiBrain` entry to `AI_BRAINS[]`
3. Add intent rule to `INTENT_RULES` if new use case
4. Map to existing Nirva agents (don't create duplicate agents)
5. Test in `shared/__tests__/brains.test.ts`

